# Analytics Dashboard – Developer Guide

## Overview

The Analytics Dashboard is a **modular, question-based system** that allows developers to add new analytics insights by simply defining SQL queries and minimal configuration—no architectural changes required.

### Key Features

- **Server-side execution**: All queries run in Server Components using service role credentials
- **RLS bypass**: Analytics queries aggregate across all data (permission-gated at page level)
- **Multiple visualizations**: Table, Bar Chart, Line Chart, Donut Chart, and Metric cards
- **Date filtering**: Shared date-range filter updates all questions in real-time
- **URL state**: Filter, tab, collection, and search state persisted in URL for shareability
- **Collections**: Questions organized into logical collections for easy navigation
- **Search**: Fuzzy search across question titles to quickly find specific insights

---

## Architecture

### File Structure

```
components/analytics/
  ├── question-card.tsx                    # Generic card renderer (Server Component)
  ├── collection-view.tsx                  # Collection navigator with search (Client Component)
  ├── date-range-filter.tsx                # Shared filter UI (Client Component)
  ├── chart-renderers/
  │   ├── bar-chart-renderer.tsx           # Recharts bar chart wrapper
  │   ├── line-chart-renderer.tsx          # Recharts line chart wrapper
  │   ├── donut-chart-renderer.tsx         # Recharts donut chart wrapper
  │   └── metric-renderer.tsx              # Large number display
  └── tabs/
      ├── store-questions.ts               # Store products collections & questions
      ├── store-tab.tsx                    # Store tab Server Component
      ├── programs-questions.ts            # Exercise programs collections & questions
      └── programs-tab.tsx                 # Programs tab Server Component

lib/supabase/
  └── analytics-client.ts                  # Service role client for analytics

types/
  └── analytics-types.ts                   # Shared TypeScript interfaces

app/dashboard/analytics/
  └── page.tsx                             # Main page with tabs + filter state
```

### Data Flow

1. **User changes date range** → Updates URL query params → Triggers re-render
2. **User selects collection or searches** → Updates URL query params → Filters visible questions
3. **Tab component (Server)** → Passes collections to `CollectionView`
4. **CollectionView (Client)** → Filters questions based on collection/search → Renders `QuestionCard` per question
5. **QuestionCard (Server)** → Executes SQL via service role client → Renders chart/table based on type
6. **Chart renderers (Client)** → Receive data as props → Render using Recharts

