## Collections Organization

Questions are organized into **collections** - logical groupings of related analytics insights within each tab. For example, the Store tab has collections for "Overview", "Inventory", and "Reviews & Ratings".

### Benefits

- **Better navigation**: Users can quickly jump to the type of insights they need
- **Logical grouping**: Related questions are kept together
- **Search functionality**: Users can search across all questions by title
- **Scalability**: Easy to add many questions without cluttering the UI

### Collection Structure

Collections are defined in the question files (e.g., `store-questions.ts`):

```typescript
export const storeCollections: QuestionCollection[] = [
	{
		id: "overview",
		name: "Overview",
		description: "Key metrics and statistics",
		questions: [
			// QuestionConfig objects here
		],
	},
	{
		id: "inventory",
		name: "Inventory",
		description: "Stock levels and inventory value",
		questions: [
			// QuestionConfig objects here
		],
	},
];
```

