## Creating a New Collection

If your question doesn't fit into existing collections, create a new one:

### Step 1: Define the Question Array

In the questions file (e.g., `store-questions.ts`), create a new array:

```typescript
const newCategoryQuestions: QuestionConfig[] = [
	{
		id: "first-question",
		title: "First Question in New Category",
		// ... rest of config
	},
	// Add more questions here
];
```

### Step 2: Add to Collections Export

Add your new collection to the exported array:

```typescript
export const storeCollections: QuestionCollection[] = [
	{
		id: "overview",
		name: "Overview",
		description: "Key metrics and statistics",
		questions: overviewQuestions,
	},
	// ... existing collections ...
	{
		id: "new-category", // Unique ID (lowercase, hyphenated)
		name: "New Category", // Display name
		description: "Description of what this collection contains", // Optional
		questions: newCategoryQuestions, // Your question array
	},
];
```

### Step 3: Test

The new collection will automatically appear as a new tab within the main tab. No other code changes needed!

**Note**: Collection tabs are displayed in the order they appear in the array. Place your new collection where it makes the most sense logically.

