## Database Setup: RPC Function (Required)

The analytics system requires a Postgres function to execute raw SQL. Run this migration in your Supabase SQL Editor:

```sql
-- Create analytics query execution function with CTE support
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION execute_analytics_query(query_text TEXT)
RETURNS JSONB
LANGUAGE plpgsql
SECURITY DEFINER
SET search_path = public
AS $$
DECLARE
  result JSONB;
BEGIN
  -- Validate that query is SELECT or WITH (CTE) only (basic security check)
  -- Both are read-only operations safe for analytics
  IF query_text !~* '^\s*(SELECT|WITH)' THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Only SELECT and WITH (CTE) queries are allowed';
  END IF;

  -- Execute the dynamic query and return results as JSONB
  EXECUTE format('SELECT COALESCE(jsonb_agg(row_to_json(t)), ''[]''::jsonb) FROM (%s) t', query_text)
  INTO result;

  RETURN result;
EXCEPTION
  WHEN OTHERS THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Query execution failed: %', SQLERRM;
END;
$$;

-- Grant execute permission to service role
GRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION execute_analytics_query(TEXT) TO service_role;

-- Add helpful comment
COMMENT ON FUNCTION execute_analytics_query IS
  'Executes read-only analytics SQL queries for the admin dashboard.
   Supports both SELECT and WITH (CTE) queries.
   MUST be called with service role credentials from Server Components only.
   Protected by ViewAnalytics permission at application level.';
```

**Why is this needed?**
Supabase doesn't allow arbitrary SQL from the client SDK. This function provides a secure way to execute analytics queries server-side with the service role key.

**Supported Query Types:**

- ✅ Direct SELECT queries: `SELECT * FROM table`
- ✅ WITH (CTE) queries: `WITH cte AS (...) SELECT ...`
- ❌ INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, DROP, etc. (blocked by validation)

