## Example: Complete Question Walkthrough

**Scenario**: We want to show "Revenue by Product Category" as a bar chart.

### 1. Write SQL

```sql
SELECT
  c.name as category_name,
  SUM(p.price * p.stock) as total_value
FROM categories c
INNER JOIN products p ON c.id = p.category_id
WHERE p.soft_deleted = false
GROUP BY c.id, c.name
ORDER BY total_value DESC
LIMIT 10
```

### 2. Test in Supabase

Run the query in SQL Editor → Verify results look correct.

### 3. Add to `store-questions.ts`

Decide this belongs in the "Inventory" collection, so add to `inventoryQuestions`:

```typescript
const inventoryQuestions: QuestionConfig[] = [
	// ... existing inventory questions ...

	{
		id: "revenue-by-category",
		title: "Revenue by Product Category",
		description: "Total potential revenue grouped by product category",
		type: "bar_chart",
		query: () => `
      SELECT
        c.name as name,
        SUM(p.price * p.stock) as value
      FROM categories c
      INNER JOIN products p ON c.id = p.category_id
      WHERE p.soft_deleted = false
      GROUP BY c.id, c.name
      ORDER BY value DESC
      LIMIT 10
    `,
		chartConfig: {
			dataKey: "value",
			nameKey: "name",
		},
	},
];
```

### 4. Done!

Refresh `/dashboard/analytics` → Select the Store tab → Select the Inventory collection → Your new question appears automatically.

